f['PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO'].max()], \n                                         labels=['Low', 'Below_Avg', 'Above_Avg', 'High'])\n```end\n\n---\n\n### Explanation for Feature Dropping\nBased on domain knowledge and statistical analysis of variance, we can drop any redundant or irrelevant features. For example:\n\n```python\n# Drop redundant column\n# Explanation: MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO has poor variability (low standard deviation and range), making it less useful for distinguishing between vehicle types.\ndf.drop(columns=['MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n", "```python\n# Step 1: Add a feature for squared compactness\ndf['COMPACTNESS_SQUARE'] = df['COMPACTNESS']**2\n# Feature description: Squared value of compactness to capture nonlinear relationships.\n# Usefulness: Vehicles with different surface areas may show distinct patterns when compactness is considered in a squared form. Nonlinear features can improve model precision by capturing complex interactions among variables.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Step 2: Create HOLLOWS_RATIO log transformation\ndf['HOLLOWS_RATIO_LOG'] = np.log(df['HOLLOWS_RATIO'])\n# Feature description: Log transformation of hollows ratio.\n# Usefulness: Log-transformed features help standardize data with a skewed distribution (HOLLOWS_RATIO appears to have tightly grouped values). This transformation could improve model learning by highlighting subtle differences in bounding polygon hollows.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Step 3: Ratio between PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO and MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO\ndf['AXIS_ASPECT_LENGTH_RATIO'] = df['PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO'] / df['MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO']\n# Feature description: Ratio between axis aspect ratio and maximum length aspect ratio.\n# Usefulness: This combined feature could highlight underlying vehicle shape discrepancies (e.g., tall, slender vehicles vs. wide, bulky ones) that aren't apparent in the original features alone.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: Skewness about the minor axis has an unusually low range (0-22), weak variability (Mean = 6.3, Std = 4.96), and likely limited predictive power for the task given other skewness measures (e.g., about the major axis) that exhibit higher variability.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column CIRCULARITY is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['CIRCULARITY'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: Circularity is highly correlated with COMPACTNESS and may be redundant. Dropping it reduces dimensionality and avoids potential multicollinearity issues in the model.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: This feature has limited utility since similar information is captured in ELONGATEDNESS and PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY, which already evaluate area relative to shape alignment.\n```end"]
