thon\n# Explanation why the column HOLLOWS_RATIO is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['HOLLOWS_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: HOLLOWS_RATIO has limited additional utility now that HOLLOWS_RATIO_LOG is already included as a more standardized and effective feature. Retaining both may add redundancy.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS has a low mean and a tight distribution (Mean: 12.57, Std: 8.61), which suggests it may hold limited variance and thus limited discriminative power as a standalone feature compared to others.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS has narrow variability (Mean: 72.1, Std: 7.05) and might not be as informative compared to the combined nonlinear or interaction features like COMPACTNESS_DISTANCE_INTERACTION.\nend\n\nWith these steps, new interactions and transformations are introduced to capture complex relationships between existing features, while redundant or less informative features are removed to reduce noise and improve the model's performance.", "python\n# Step 1: Create a feature for compactness-to-distance circularity ratio\ndf['COMPACTNESS_DISTANCE_RATIO'] = df['COMPACTNESS'] / df['DISTANCE_CIRCULARITY']\n# Feature description: Ratio between compactness and distance circularity.\n# Usefulness: This feature captures how compactness interacts with the circular distribution of the shape. Vehicles with more irregular shapes may show distinct behaviors in this ratio compared to more symmetric vehicles, providing useful context for classification.\nend\n\npython\n# Step 2: Add a feature for elongatedness-to-scatter ratio\ndf['ELONGATEDNESS_SCATTER_RATIO'] = df['ELONGATEDNESS'] / df['SCATTER_RATIO']\n# Feature description: Ratio between elongatedness and scatter ratio.\n# Usefulness: This feature blends two shape-related metrics, highlighting how stretched and uneven a vehicle silhouette appears. It could help differentiate vehicle types like buses (long, evenly shaped) from vans (shorter, boxier shapes).\nend\n\npython\n# Step 3: Log transformation of SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS\ndf['SCALED_MINOR_VARIANCE_LOG'] = np.log(df['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS'])\n# Feature description: Log transformation of scaled variance along the minor axis.\n# Usefulness: This transformation helps manage skewness in the feature, emphasizing relative differences in the spread along the minor axis. It could enhance the model's ability to distinguish shape characteristics that align with certain vehicle types.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column HOLLOWS_RATIO is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['HOLLOWS_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: HOLLOWS_RATIO has limited variability and is now redundant, as HOLLOWS_RATIO_LOG provides a more robust representation for modeling and interpretation purposes.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS has narrow variability (Mean = 12.57, Std = 8.61) compared to other features and contributes limited discriminative power to the classification task.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO overlaps conceptually with AXIS_ASPECT_LENGTH_RATIO and ELONGATEDNESS_SCATTER_RATIO, making it redundant and less impactful as a standalone feature.\nend", "python\n# Step 1: Create a feature for compactness normalized by distance circularity (ratio)\ndf['COMPACTNESS_DISTANCE_RATIO'] = df['COMPACTNESS'] / df['DISTANCE_CIRCULARITY']\n# Feature description: Ratio of compactness to distance circularity.\n# Usefulness: This ratio could reveal how compactness scales with circularity and may help differentiate vehicles with similar shapes but differing boundary characteristics.\nend\n\npython\n# Step 2: Square root transformation of SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS\ndf['SCALED_VARIANCE_MINOR_SQRT'] = np.sqrt(df['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS'])\n# Feature description: Square root of scaled variance along the minor axis.\n# Usefulness: This transformation smoothens the wide range of scaled variance while retaining relative relationships, potentially enhancing the model's understanding of variations in vehicle shapes.\nend\n\npython\n# Step 3: Interaction feature between HOLLOWS_RATIO_LOG and ELONGATEDNESS\ndf['HOLLOWS_ELONGATED_INTERACTION'] = df['HOLLOWS_RATIO_LOG'] * df['ELONGATEDNESS']\n# Feature description: Interaction between the log-transformed hollows ratio and elongatedness.\n# Usefulness: This feature captures how internal structure (hollows) interacts with the exterior elongation, potentially highlighting unique shape characteristics across vehicle types.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS exhibits limited variability (Mean: 12.57, Std: 8.61) and likely provides less discriminative power when compared to other features with broader distributions and contextual relationships.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column HOLLOWS_RATIO is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['HOLLOWS_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: HOLLOWS_RATIO_LOG, a log-transformed version of HOLLOWS_RATIO, is already included and provides a more standardized and useful representation. Retaining the original feature adds redundancy.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: The newly added interaction and ratio features (e.g., HOLLOWS_ELONGATED_INTERACTION) incorporate aspects of scaled radius of gyration in conjunction with other features, making SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION less necessary on its own.\nend", "python\n# Step 1: Interaction feature between DISTANCE_CIRCULARITY and ELONGATEDNESS\ndf['DISTANCE_ELONGATEDNESS_INTERACTION'] = df['DISTANCE_CIRCULARITY'] * df['ELONGATEDNESS']\n# Feature description: Interaction between distance circularity and elongatedness.\n# Usefulness: This feature explores the relationship between how circular a vehicle's silhouette is and how elongated it becomes. Vehicles like buses (long and less circular) versus vans (boxy and elongated) may show distinct patterns here, enabling better classification.\nend\n\npython\n# Step 2: Log transformation of SCATTER_RATIO\ndf['SCATTER_RATIO_LOG'] = np.log(df['SCATTER_RATIO'])\n# Feature description: Log transformation of the scatter ratio.\n# Usefulness: SCATTER_RATIO has a relatively wide range of values and potential skewness. A logarithmic transformation standardizes this range, capturing subtle variations in inertia ratios that might differentiate vehicle types.\nend\n\npython\n# Step 3: Ratio feature between PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY and SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION\ndf['RECTANGULARITY_GYRATION_RATIO'] = df['PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY'] / df['SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION']\n# Feature description: Ratio of principal axis rectangularity to scaled radius of gyration.\n# Usefulness: Combining rectangularity and gyration provides a feature that quantifies how tightly the vehicle's shape fits within its bounding axes. Specific vehicle silhouettes may exhibit distinctive ratios.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column HOLLOWS_RATIO is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['HOLLOWS_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: HOLLOWS_RATIO_LOG already captures the information in HOLLOWS_RATIO in a more normalized format. Retaining the original feature is redundant and could lead to noise in the model.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS shows limited variability and has a narrow range. It likely offers negligible predictive power compared to other features with higher information gain.\nend\n\npython\n# Explanation why the column SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION'], inplace=True)\n# Reason: The newly generated feature RECTANGULARITY_GYRATION_RATIO integrates the useful aspects of SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION with contextual relationships to PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY, making this feature redundant.\nend", "python\n# Step 1: Create square root transformation of COMPACTNESS\ndf['COMPACTNESS_SQRT'] = np.sqrt(df['COMPACTNESS'])\n# Feature description: Square root of compactness.\n# Usefulness: The square root transformation reduces the impact of larger compactness values and may better capture subtle differences across vehicle types with similar compactness but different shapes. This non-linear transformation can improve the model's sensitivity to variability.\nend\n\npython\n# Step 2: Interaction feature between PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO and SCATTER_RATIO\ndf['PR_SCATTER_INTERACTION'] = df['PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO'] * df['SCATTER_RATIO']\n# Feature description: Interaction between primary axis aspect ratio and scatter ratio.\n# Usefulness: This feature combines the dimensional alignment of a vehicle's primary axis with the inertia distribution, which might highlight shape differences between vehicle classes (e.g., compact cars vs. large buses or vans).\nend\n\npython\n# Step 3: Log transformation of SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MAJOR_AXIS\ndf['SCALED_MAJOR_VARIANCE_LOG'] = np.log(df['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MAJOR_AXIS'])\n# Feature description: Log transformation of scaled variance along the major axis.\n# Usefulness: This transformation helps stabilize the variance for features with a wide range by compressing larger values. It can improve the understanding of how variance along the major axis differs across